WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.277
OT disruption can produce consequences far beyond an unavailable application.

00:00:04.277 --> 00:00:08.872
Downtime may stop production, damage material, delay shipments, interrupt public service,

00:00:08.872 --> 00:00:11.378
or require expensive restart and cleanup.

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:16.390
The financial impact can increase with every hour the process remains unstable.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.732
Safety and environmental consequences may dominate the decision.

00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:22.238
Loss of control, alarms, ventilation, cooling,

00:00:22.238 --> 00:00:27.668
or utility support can force a shutdown even when equipment still appears operational.

00:00:27.668 --> 00:00:32.681
Continuity planning defines conservative thresholds before teams face those choices under pressure.

00:00:32.681 --> 00:00:35.187
Supply chains can amplify local disruption.

00:00:35.187 --> 00:00:38.111
A single unavailable plant, terminal, treatment facility,

00:00:38.111 --> 00:00:41.870
or distribution node may affect customers and downstream operations.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:46.047
Contractual commitments, regulatory reporting, and public trust add further impact.

00:00:46.047 --> 00:00:48.971
Cyber incidents are one cause among many.

00:00:48.971 --> 00:00:51.060
Ransomware, destructive activity, credential compromise,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:55.237
or loss of remote access may interrupt visibility and control.

00:00:55.237 --> 00:00:59.414
Equipment failure, fire, flood, severe weather, utility loss, communications outages,

00:00:59.414 --> 00:01:02.755
and unavailable vendors can create similar continuity demands.

00:01:02.755 --> 00:01:04.008
Events can combine.

00:01:04.008 --> 00:01:07.768
A natural hazard may reduce staffing while damaging communications.

00:01:07.768 --> 00:01:13.198
A cyber incident may occur during planned maintenance when redundancy is already limited.

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:16.957
Plans should avoid assuming that every control, person, supplier,

00:01:16.957 --> 00:01:19.463
and backup remains available at once.

00:01:19.463 --> 00:01:21.134
Continuity investment reduces improvisation.

00:01:21.134 --> 00:01:24.894
It identifies priorities, alternate modes, recovery resources, decision authority,

00:01:24.894 --> 00:01:26.982
and communication before an incident.

00:01:26.982 --> 00:01:30.741
The value is not a promise of zero downtime;

00:01:30.741 --> 00:01:36.589
it is the ability to protect people and the mission while making recovery faster,

00:01:36.589 --> 00:01:38.260
safer, and more predictable.
